KG42.register("clusters-321f963bdf628f09c09b6f8d",{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v142-d-K004","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","label":"LMO-coordinated bilateral allocation, price formation, and trade execution.","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"LMO-coordinated bilateral allocation, price formation, and trade execution.","market_meaning":"The LMO takes the submitted total P2P buy and sell quantities as input, coordinates bilateral allocation, energy matching, and price formation for local energy commodities, and links P2P execution and residual grid trading. Direct instance evidence for using the transaction price in execution is limited to the sample period in Fig.12; the existing chains are not yet sufficient to give complete mathematical closure and general settlement obligations.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M03-lem"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","pricing","activation"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"Bilateral quantities and prices come from the same LMO problem, and the execution chain retains its repeated constraints and added procedural explanations. The closure from total quantity to allocation among multiple counterparties, the role of multipliers, the transcription of the time factor, and the price interface remain unresolved; a price application or price assumption in a numerical example is not generalized into a universal payment rule.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Commodity definition, bilateral allocation, balance price, and LMO execution jointly describe a market function from existing bids to transaction outcomes. Bid optimization serves only as a shared input interface; repeated constraints and objectives remain traceable and are not counted as independent rules or a second clearing.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the LMO responsibility, bilateral allocation limits, energy matching, and local optimization; this is the allocation-side core of this cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplement the price and multiplier meanings of the same clearing problem, without counting a second clearing optimization."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplement LMO execution, application of the sample transaction price, and residual-grid conditions; the repeated bid and bilateral constraints serve only as execution-side representations of the same content."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Define the local energy commodities involved in bilateral buying and selling and their quantities; a commodity declaration is not counted separately as an operating rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the determined total purchase bid quantity and its DOE scope; the primary attribution is in v142-d-K003, and local clearing is not reinterpreted as bid optimization."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the signed total sale bid quantity, the joint bidding context, and the total P2P balance; the primary attribution is in v142-d-K003."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-Ppb"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Ppb_jt","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that the bilateral purchase limit uses the total purchase quantity from the bidding stage; this quantity moves from the bidding decision into the clearing input, and both local objects are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x-Pps-jt"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Pps_jt","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The source uses the signed total sale bid quantity for the bilateral sale lower bound; retain the non-positive sign and the status factor, and do not change the sale limit into an upper bound on a positive quantity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::var_Ppb_ji_t","v141-c-R005::x::var_Pps_ji_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The peer buy and sell quantities in the commodity definition correspond to the quantities handled by bilateral allocation; the units and sign domains missing from the definition remain retained according to the original object, and no new scientific edge from commodity to clearing is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R005::x::var_lambda_cijt"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36"],"rationale":"The source links the bilateral quantities of the same LMO optimization with the multiplier prices of the balance constraints; this is an assembly of allocation and price functions, and whether the multiplier solution is closed remains listed as a gap."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::var_Ppb_ji_t","v141-c-R005::x::var_Pps_ji_t","v141-c-R005::x::var_C_ji_t","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X003","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X004","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g03-e014"],"rationale":"The allocation and execution representations use the same bilateral quantities, transaction status, and matching constraints; this does not prove that there is a separate physical activation model, nor does it fill in metering or delivery verification."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e013","v141-b-g03-e014"],"rationale":"The general framework states that the LMO forms prices, and Fig.12 states that the buying and selling at sample t=39 are executed at the optimal P2P price; the price application in this interface retains that instance scope and does not derive universal settlement or payment obligations."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C007","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C009","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31"],"rationale":"The execution chain restates the existing DOE limits and total P2P balance and supplements residual-grid trading and the assumption when there is no P2P; the repeated parts do not add rules, and procedural assumptions do not automatically become mathematical equations in the objective."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The same demand-bid node is repeatedly referenced in the bidding, allocation, and execution chains; the display identity is unified, but edges with different objectives are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The three references are the same frozen supply-bid node; the original limiting edges and local constraints are each retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R009::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36"],"rationale":"The quantity and price sides reference the same local clearing node and do not constitute two independent clearing activities."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g03-e014"],"rationale":"Both refer to the LMO coordination role in the source; only existing node references are unified, and it is not equated with the DSO."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M05","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e013","v141-b-g03-e014"],"rationale":"Price formation and sample execution reference the same local price node; the scope of the execution instance is not expanded by the display unification."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-Ppb","v141-c-R004::x::x-Ppb-jt","v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Ppb_jt","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The source explicitly identifies the same total P2P purchase bid quantity; the decision quantity in bidding, the given limit in clearing, and the reference role in the execution chain remain independent."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x-Pps-jt","v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Pps_jt","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"Both are the same signed total P2P sale bid quantity; the role difference between the decision quantity and the clearing input is retained, and they are not rewritten as one object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-Pgb","v141-c-R004::x::x-Pgb-jt","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E30"],"rationale":"Both correspond to the upper-grid purchase quantity; the execution-side reference does not additionally prove measured delivery or performance."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x-Pgs-jt","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X007"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E30"],"rationale":"The bidding-side and execution-side representations of the same signed upper-grid sale quantity; the original non-positive sign and conditional domain are both retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-DOE","v141-c-R004::theta::theta-Phat-jt","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30"],"rationale":"Local references to the same allocated DOE; R003 covers only the positive-value import branch, while other objects cover both branches, and this difference in applicability cannot be erased."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001","v141-c-R005::x::var_Ppb_ji_t","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X003","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-Ppb-jit"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e015"],"rationale":"The explicit transaction direction and indices support that they are the same bilateral purchase quantity family; the variable domains, missing unit entries, and sample unit bases of each chain are retained separately, and the Fig.12 units are not generalized to all objects."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M12","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X002","v141-c-R005::x::var_Pps_ji_t","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34"],"rationale":"All three objects define a quantity family in the direction of sale from j to i; the reverse-direction sale quantity under the fixed index of R009 is not included, nor are the buy and sell directions treated as equal."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M13","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::var_C_ji_t","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"The same binary transaction-status quantity controls the corresponding bilateral purchase and sale limits; the local bindings in allocation and execution are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M14","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::var_lambda_cijt","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36"],"rationale":"The source points to the same balance multiplier and bilateral price object; this correspondence does not confirm that it should serve as an ordinary decision variable in minimization, and its solution role remains unresolved."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M15","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Lambda_pb_jt","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-pb-jt"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36"],"rationale":"The purchase price coefficient in the same Eq. (39); it is not merged with the market price in Eq. (28) or the output multiplier price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M16","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Lambda_ps_it","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-ps-it"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36"],"rationale":"The sale price coefficient in the same Eq. (39); the seller index and input role are retained, and it is not equivalent to the clearing output price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M17","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::theta-tau","v141-c-R005::theta::theta_tau","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-tau"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E35"],"rationale":"Both reference the time-period factor of the same framework; the quantity correspondence does not resolve the dispute over its multiplication scope in Eq. (39), nor does it supply a numerical duration."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M18","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30"],"rationale":"The two expressions give the same three-term purchase limit under the same positive-DOE condition; the bidding and execution members and roles are retained, and the repeated transcription is not counted as a newly added constraint."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M19","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30"],"rationale":"Both expressions are the same sale component and aggregate limit under the non-positive-DOE condition; the bindings at different stages remain traceable."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M20","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C007"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g03-e011"],"rationale":"Both represent the total P2P balance of Eq. (35) in the source, but their explicit quantifiers for the sale-sign condition and their stage-binding formulations differ; retain both versions, without choosing a representative or counting an additional independent rule."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M21","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"Both come from equation (36); the execution version additionally writes the binary domain explicitly, and the local variable role of the total declared quantity differs, so they are retained as different representations of the same bound."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M22","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33"],"rationale":"Both come from the signed sales bound in equation (37); the representational differences of the explicit binary domain and of the parameter or variable roles are retained, and the scientific objects are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M23","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e002","v141-b-g03-e004"],"rationale":"All three point to the bilateral matching in equation (38); the explicit sales sign condition, the price multiplier association, and the local variable references differ; the alternative expressions are retained and the reverse index is left to manual verification."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M24","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36"],"rationale":"The currently frozen expressions all transcribe the same equation (39) and its constraint scope; no representative is selected, the source time-factor difference and the multiplier-role doubt are still retained, and they cannot be counted as two optimization rules."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"All source support in this cluster is unaudited evidence permitted by the experiment; the existing C2 bindings and revision requests also do not mean that an independent scientific review has been completed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e002","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004","v141-b-g03-e009","v141-b-g03-e011","v141-b-g03-e013","v141-b-g03-e014","v141-b-g03-e015"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the source, transcription, and assembly interpretation chain by chain; retain all original objects, and do not claim that the B audit, independent C2 review, or scientific acceptance has been completed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The pairwise allocation bounds only restrict each bilateral quantity; they do not provide a closure condition between the bilateral total across multiple counterparties for each prosumer and the total declared quantity. Bilateral matching and total-declaration balance are insufficient to guarantee that the actual allocation total still satisfies the total declaration or the DOE.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-Ppb","v141-c-R004::x::x-Pps-jt","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g03-e013"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether a consistency constraint between the bilateral total and the total declared quantity has been omitted, and have C add source-supported content; the multi-counterparty example in Fig.12 cannot replace general mathematical closure."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"λ appears as an operating variable in the frozen catalog, and the source also calls it the Lagrange multiplier of the balance constraint. If equation (38) is still enforced, this multiplier term in the objective disappears, and the price cannot be determined solely from the listed primal minimization; the dual direction after relaxing the constraint, other constraint multipliers, and the treatment of KKT applicability under binary states are also not fully given.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::var_lambda_cijt","v141-c-R005::x::var_C_ji_t","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e004"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream is to check the primal problem, the Lagrangian form, the primal and dual solution directions, and how binary states are fixed or relaxed, and to clarify the price-recovery conditions; D does not correct the frozen objective or write out a KKT system."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"E35 places τ outside the entire summation bracket, whereas the transcription in g03-e003 places it inside the multiplier term; the two frozen objectives currently use the former scope, and the difference between the sources remains unresolved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R005::theta::theta_tau","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-tau"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g03-e003"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the typesetting of equation (39) and the exact multiplication scope of τ, then have upstream revise the transcription; the two frozen objectives and the source difference are currently retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G05","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Equation (37) defines quantity as sale from j to i, while equations (38) to (39) use the reverse pairing from i to j. Under fixed j and i, the sales object of R009 should not be directly equated with same-direction sales objects of other chains, and the existing local references do not yet explicitly express the index permutation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::var_Pps_ji_t","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X004","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-Pps-ijt","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34","v141-b-g02-E35"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the sales subscripts and OCR, and clarify the index permutation of the quantity family, the transaction direction, and the corresponding seller declaration bound; do not merge reverse sales quantities and same-direction sales quantities into the same fixed-index object."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G06","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The market price Λ in equation (28), the buy and sell price coefficients in equation (39), and the output λ assume different local roles. g03-e009 only gives the equal-price assumption in a numerical example, and it involves the seller index; a general price identity or feedback dependency cannot be established from it.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::theta-Llem-jt","v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Lambda_pb_jt","v141-c-R005::theta::theta_Lambda_ps_it","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-pb-jt","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-ps-it","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e009"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Confirm the source of the input price in the general model, the participant index, and the relationship to the output price; the example assumption remains a local condition, and no price-update loop is added and these quantities are not merged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G07","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The residual grid trading in the execution chain and the fact that the grid quantity equals the DOE when there is no P2P are procedural statements; they are not enforced by the current mathematical bounds, and a complete interface for determining the residual quantity from the total bilateral transactions is not given; for export, the comparison direction or magnitude meaning of the source text's statement of being less than the DOE still needs verification.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C009","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the definition of the residual quantity, the constraint relationship between the no-P2P assumption and the optimization, and the meaning of the export sign, and have upstream complete the source-supported interface; do not change the bounds into equalities on its own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G08","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Fig.12 reports only the sample trade quantity in kW and the price in ¢; this is insufficient to determine the conversion between energy and power in the general objective, or the dimensional relationships of the price coefficients, multipliers, and τ. The existing unit interpretation of R009 remains frozen but still needs verification, and the sample units cannot be used to fill empty values in other chains.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::var_Ppb_ji_t","v141-c-R005::theta::theta_tau","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X003","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-Ppb-jit","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-cijt","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Lambda-pb-jt","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e015"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the complete units and normalization basis of the general trade quantity, the time-period duration, and each price term; before upstream confirmation, retain the original units and empty values and do not perform global unit unification."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G09","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The dedicated node proposal for the mismatch-minimization objective has still not been approved; this cluster can only reference the existing local clearing object and cannot rename that objective as social welfare maximization. Transaction execution also cannot replace the EV charging and discharging and SOC control for which a chain is still missing.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R006::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004","v141-b-g03-e012"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-p02-p2p-mismatch-clearing","v141-b-g03-p03-ev-activation"],"required_work":"The objective and EV control node proposals are to be handled manually; if the scope is extended to EV resource management, upstream is to add the corresponding chain; currently only the transaction execution scope is retained and no new graph object is inserted."}]},"rule_refs":["43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R005","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R009","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R006","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R010","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R003","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3fcd5e2d02ec7c3f","COMP-58a3c8caf66a5d40","COMP-5ed84d11cdfb4465","COMP-ae4944a1a62bf858","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-cff64e1ff77ba8f0"]});
